==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|[[hebamme]] {{q|15th century}}, [[heveamme]] {{q|13 ct.}}}}, from {{inh|de|goh|hevanna||midwife}}, later altered to {{m|de||Hebamme}} to resemble {{m|de|Amme||wet nurse}} ({{m|gmh|amme}}). This development is still reflected in modern German, inasmuch as the word can either be pronounced as a compound ("''Heb-Amme''") or as one word ("''Hebamme''").

